<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Summoning Resistance</h1>
<p>Sphere: Protection Sphere
Class: none (no guild teaches it)
Mana: 20
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast summoning resistance &lt;target&gt;
<a cmd='#'>cast summoning resistance</a>   (on yourself)
</pre>
<p>The caster traces a circle around the target, and raises their summoning 
sphere for about ten minutes. Your ability in a sphere also protects you 
against its spells (see <a cmd='#'>Help Spheres</a>), so the target resists summoning 
spells better, such as cone of shards and meteor shower. The better your 
protection sphere, the bigger the raise, up to ten points and a little 
more for a master.
</p><p>It doesn't add up: cast on someone who already has it, the magic just 
dissipates. You must be standing. No guild teaches it, but it turns up on 
potions, wands and scrolls among random treasure.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Summoning Sphere</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Acid Resistance</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Protection Sphere</a>
</pre>




</div>